LMAO. 💀 So the AI didn't invent the architecture. You'd already solved the difficult networking problem, and the AI essentially took your working prototype and turned it into a more elaborate, reproducible deployment.

That changes how I interpret the entire README.

Your original architecture was already quite clever:

    Run OpenConnect inside a Fedora container, keeping the corporate VPN isolated from the host.

    Put Warpgate in the same network namespace so it could reach corporate servers through the tunnel.

    Access internal servers through Warpgate's SSH bastion and OpenShift console endpoints through its HTTP bastion.

    Keep the host's normal internet connection intact.

That's the fundamental architecture. The AI didn't discover some magical networking trick. You'd already done the important part.
